\paragraph{Within-pool controlled comparison.}
\label{sec:within_pool}
Within-pool analysis confirms slope consistency across pools (permutation $p \approx 0.60$; Appendix~\ref{app:within-pool-method}). The 80-relation extreme-batch gap (\S\ref{sec:bcs_controlled}) reflects wider BCS range, not stronger per-unit sensitivity.

\paragraph{Practical magnitude.}
\label{sec:practical_magnitude}
\looseness=-1
Direct regression on 100 random 16-type batches within the 80-relation pool yields a restricted-range estimate ($r = -0.22$, $R^2 \approx 0.05$, $p = 0.027$) due to narrow BCS range. The pooled semipartial $R^2 = 0.273$ ($n = 204$) is the primary estimate; DocRED's $R^2 = 0.578$ is inflated by multicollinearity (semipartial $R^2_{\text{BCS}} = 0.056$; Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_partial_corr}). Amplification from pairwise $r^2 \approx 1.5\%$ to batch-level ${\sim}$27\% reflects correlated confusable-type interactions compounding within shared prompts \citep{robinson-1950-ecological,baan-2023-ecological} (${\sim}3\times$; Appendix~\ref{app:aggregation-sim}).

